package IfErrNotEqualNil

/// Go compatibility wrapper for error handling.
///
/// Oct does not let an unhandled error reach a parameter. By the time this
/// function is called, the caller has already written `?`, `!` or `match`,
/// and nothing is left to check. The function returns its argument.
///
/// Provided for compatibility-oriented workflows.
template fn IfErrNotEqualNil<T>(value: T) -> T {
    return value
}
